1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,000
Hong Kong, 2026

2
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,300
No crash. No dent. Then the claims.

3
00:00:05,300 --> 00:00:07,500
Arrests, and not only in Hong Kong

4
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:11,200
Hundreds of cases. Millions claimed.

5
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:13,800
How do you prove a negative?

6
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:17,100
Prove the lane was empty

7
00:00:17,100 --> 00:00:17,700
A lane change across a solid line

8
00:00:17,700 --> 00:00:19,500
Someone nearby is filming

9
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:20,000
Weeks later…

10
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:21,500
A claim: “I was right behind you”

11
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:23,200
No crash, so nothing was recorded

12
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:24,600
Turn the claim into a zone

13
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:25,700
Record where radar saw free space

14
00:00:25,700 --> 00:00:26,800
Seal the record in the car

15
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:28,000
Share only the claimed zone

16
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Refute only when a miss is unlikely

17
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,200
Same claim, two cars

18
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:33,400
One has nothing. One has evidence.

19
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:35,000
Keep evidence of empty space

20
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:36,700
The car crosses the solid line

21
00:00:36,700 --> 00:00:37,600
Radar logs free space, sealed

22
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:39,700
Replay: was the claimed zone empty?

23
00:00:39,700 --> 00:00:40,400
Observed empty: claim refuted

24
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:42,000
What if a truck hides the zone?

25
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:43,900
Not seen means no refutation

26
00:00:43,900 --> 00:00:45,500
A zone, healthy sensors, a seal

27
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:47,000
Nothing hidden, every verdict graded

28
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:48,900
Each part tested in simulation

29
00:00:48,900 --> 00:00:50,400
If the car can’t see, it says so

30
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:51,900
Real claims are confirmed, too

31
00:00:51,900 --> 00:00:55,600
Simulated results

32
00:00:55,600 --> 00:00:58,800
Evidence by design, not by video

